-- Rollback: DELETE FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class LIKE 'rt-page-%' AND module = 'runtime-liveness-v1'
-- PAGE-LIVENESS-1 (2026-10-13, pillars core and reach, metric runtime_verified_share_24h). The fleet probed each worker's
-- /health from outside the Cloudflare account (rt-live-*, PROBE-TRANSPORT-MONOCULTURE-1) and five hosts' front pages
-- (rt-papers, rt-q08, rt-ipatent ...), but none of the pages readers, crawlers and feed readers actually load: the paper
-- list, a paper page with its Google Scholar tags, the sitemaps and RSS feeds, ask.qwav.tech, qwav.org, reading.q08.org,
-- the KPI page the owner reads, the subscribe and work-with-me pages. A route detached from a host, a broken template or
-- an empty feed showed up only when a person noticed. Each contract below GETs one page from the GitHub-hosted runner
-- (scripts/remediation_consumer.py, runner-https: GET only, allowlisted hosts, token-only observations) hourly, checks a
-- marker that only the working page carries, and files RUNTIME-PROBE-FAIL-1 after three straight failures; the autoclose
-- trigger closes that issue on the first pass. Markers were read from the live pages on 2026-10-13 06:20 UTC (all 200,
-- under 2 s). runtime_verified_share_24h was 8.7 (trigger fires under 10): of 8455 verifications in 24 h, 737 were
-- runtime and 7718 read D1 or the source. Twenty-one hourly page probes add about 670 runtime observations a day, so the
-- share settles near 15; the rest of the gap is fix confirmations on D1 (219 of 5809 issue verifications were runtime),
-- which a probe on a page cannot honestly replace.
